{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Do not be agitated on the way.</b> Do not engage in a matter of halakhah, lest the way become turbulent against you. Another interpretation: do not take large strides, and enter the city while it is still warm. And according to the plain sense of Scripture, one may say: since they were ashamed, he was concerned lest they quarrel on the way about the matter of his sale, arguing with one another and saying, 'Through you he was sold — you told evil talk about him and caused us to hate him.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:38.177566663Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}